{
  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.629 acc, only +0.038 over RNA-only config_018 (0.591), while image-only config_009 is weak (0.332). This suggests RNA dominates and the image contribution is modest, but it is unclear whether the modest multimodal gain is a ceiling or an artifact of the simple concat fusion. Question: config_020 is identical to config_001 except fusion is changed from concat to weighted, making it a clean single-variable test of whether the fusion strategy is bottlenecking the image signal. Why best next step: it directly isolates the fusion effect without confounding changes to encoder, aggregation, or profile setting. A positive result would justify investing in stronger image encoders or transformer aggregation; a null result would indicate the image contribution is inherently limited with current encoders, redirecting budget toward RNA encoder improvements (scgpt, scvi_n200). Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about where to focus remaining experiments."
}

